## Source-Lineage Conservation

The V1.4 predecessor remains immutable. Its 36 parser-visible rows, 34 aromatic rows, five spatial planes, four connected lavender states, pressure/release pair, dry recurrence system, and one-musk policy are all preserved. S4 adds one function-owned spice row and rebases only DEP. No wood is added because no missing wood function has been physically demonstrated; a simultaneous wood change would confound the spice question.

| Lineage item | Predecessor | S4 | Disposition |
|---|---:|---:|---|
| parser-visible rows | 36 | 37 | all 36 retained; one spice ADD |
| aromatic rows | 34 | 35 | no aromatic removal |
| raw concentrate | 6,000 uL | 6,000 uL | constant total |
| spatial planes | 5 | 5 | KEEP |
| connected subject states | 4 | 4 | KEEP; spice modifies transitions |
| musk rows | 1 | 1 | KEEP Romandolide only |
| wood configuration | unchanged | unchanged | KEEP; causal isolation |
| DEP | 975 uL | 965 uL | REBASE by -10 uL |

The DHP2025 source is used only as a structural grammar: one lavender subject in connected states, spatial planes, recurrence, pressure/release, and an identity-bearing base. No donor perfume ingredient identity or proprietary reconstruction is imported.

## Candidate Theory

**Name:** Bergamot-Juniper Snap.  
**One sentence:** the bergamot-silk control receives a deliberately tiny juniper snap that punctures softness at the front, then disappears into the same rosemary-terpinyl-lavender stem language.  
**New spice function:** a tiny pinene/berry snap that restores athletic front tension to soft bergamot-linalyl silk and joins Rosemary to late Terpinyl Acetate.  
**Hedonic hypothesis:** A short cool snap may make the softest citrus candidate more kinetic and re-smellable while preserving its seamless fabric and yielding base. This is a design hypothesis, not a sensory result.  
**Failure veto:** gin, pine cleaner, Christmas conifer, turpentine, tonic, dry terpene glare, or juniper leadership.

### Alternative gate

Clary Sage would duplicate lavender/coumarin and increase barbershop risk; Cardamom could become a recognizable spice; Ginger could make bergamot beverage-like; Black/Pink Pepper would revive a rejected pepper object, and Pink Pepper stock physics/composite/basis remain unresolved.

### Literature and local-data boundary

[Primary source](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/21104523/): GC-MS studies of Juniperus communis berry oil report alpha-pinene dominance with myrcene, sabinene, limonene, beta-pinene, and germacrene variation, supporting a low-dose pinene/berry snap and a strict no-gin boundary.

Juniper Berry EO is current neat inventory and has an exact-name composite model, but the data spine contains duplicate canonical records and 10-ppb ODT while ODT_DATA records 15 ppb. A nominal 10% v/v DEP working stock is used only as a future theory representation because 10 uL neat is predicted to be too forceful; the stock does not exist and preparation is not authorized.

Literature composition is not silently assigned to the user's bottle. Species/chemotype, extraction, supplier lot, oxidation state, bottle headspace, current safety documentation, and behavior in this formula remain lot-specific or HOLD.

## One Subject / Multiple States

| State | Same lavender subject in this state | Material transition owner |
|---|---|---|
| cool bergamot-juniper snap | literal lavender stem is cut by the retained citrus plus the new spice, warm mandarin reflection, rosemary, aldehyde, Scentenal, and DHM | Bergamot FCF + Juniper Berry EO + Linalyl Acetate |
| moving premium lavender silk | BONTAUX lavender becomes flexible aromatic cloth rather than a separate citrus-spice top | Linalyl Acetate, linalools, Hedione HC, Dihydrojasmone, Mayol |
| yielding mineral wood under retained dry tension | the same cloth bends through wet-mineral tension into yielding sandal face, dense fiber, cedar grain, and root | AIMI, Helional/Cyclamen, Sandalore, Ebanol, Javanol, cedar/vetiver |
| dry lavender-hay-moss stem/grain residue | the opening's stem/fiber direction returns as hay, moss, cedar, vetiver, and woody fabric rather than persistent fruit or spice | Terpinyl Acetate, Coumarin, Evernyl, cedar/vetiver, Romandolide |

**Invariant identity cue:** dry lavender stem over yielding pale wood with a narrow mineral line. The spice may shape the route but may not become the perfume's best name.

## Spatial and Pressure/Release Architecture

| Plane | Owners | Required effect | Stop rule |
|---|---|---|---|
| front glint | Bergamot FCF, Juniper Berry EO, Red Mandarin, Rosemary, Aldehyde C10, Scentenal | directional citrus-spice motion around lavender | reject if citrus, spice, cleaner, beverage, culinary, or tonic becomes the first object |
| near body | two lavenders, DHM, Linalyl Acetate | athletic lavender remains the first full object | reject shower gel, deodorant, barbershop, or medicinal drift |
| living middle | linalool pair, Hedione HC, Hexyl Salicylate, Dihydrojasmone, Mayol, Helional/Cyclamen, AIMI | moving fabric with simultaneous air, tenderness, and mineral tension | reject detergent, hollow radiance, muguet, or aquatic product |
| rear contour | Iso E, Ambrofix, Sandalore, Javanol, Ebanol, cedar, vetiver, Cashmeran, Timberol, Azarbre | cool pressure around yielding warm grain | reject ambrox wall, burning wood, metallic sandal, or rigid base |
| skin/fabric echo | Terpinyl Acetate, Coumarin, Evernyl, cedar/vetiver, Romandolide | late lavender-stem-hay-moss-grain recognition | reject anonymous woody musk, laundry, sweet tonka, or chypre |

**Pressure module:** Juniper microdose + DHM + Rosemary + Scentenal + Helional/Cyclamen + Iso E + Ambrofix + Timberol.  
**Release module:** Bergamot FCF + Red Mandarin + BONTAUX lavender + linalyl system + Hedione HC + Mayol + AIMI + Sandalore/Ebanol + Azarbre + Romandolide.  
**Collision interval:** opening through 30 minutes, with the spice expected to change the handoff rather than form a second accord.  
**Expected re-smell event:** sharp top pressure dissolves into premium lavender fabric while the base preserves a transformed stem/fiber echo.  
**Wood decision:** unchanged for causal isolation. The existing base already owns perspective, mineral pressure, yielding face, radiant vein, dense fiber, literal grain, root, tactile flex, distal edge, warm countercurve, and outward fabric. “More depth” alone is not a missing function.

