### Nominal stock and ppm accounting

- Juniper Berry EO: 10 uL raw at nominal 10% v/v in DEP; future working stock; preparation NOT AUTHORIZED; 1 uL nominal active-equivalent = 166.7 nominal active ppm in concentrate.
- Bergamot FCF: 60 uL neat = 10,000 nominal active ppm in concentrate.
- Total nominal aromatic-equivalent: 4,443.2 uL-equivalent = 740,533.3 nominal active ppm.
- Total nominal carrier-equivalent: 1,556.8 uL-equivalent.
- DHM remains 200 uL neat = 33,333.3 active ppm in concentrate.
- Evernyl remains 25 uL of nominal 20% DPG stock = 5 uL nominal active-equivalent = 833.3 nominal active ppm.
- Exact ppm w/w is HOLD because densities and several stock bases are unresolved.
- The Juniper working stock would require at least 100 uL neat parent plus 900 uL verified DEP for a nominal 10% v/v bottle, labeled and homogenized. That preparation is future work and is not authorized.

